{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"stop","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"The journey has been ordinary and, despite the change in weather, very bearable; on Sunday the sky was overcast — it rained a few times — until Jüterbog; then on Monday, after midday, I arrived in Herzberg, where I had a country parson invite his niece to keep me company until Dresden; she was not ugly, already well into her years, so insignificant and Saxonly polite that I had little more desire or occasion to speak than if I had been traveling alone; so I think nothing ill of this company; had I, however, become a proper Englishman on my travels, I would not have let myself be talked out of it, but would have kept to myself; but as one is still a bit of a German, I could not refuse, and besides — as we Swabians say — I bought the cat in the sack, and the result was not uneven, but insignificant. — Upon arrival I went straight to the inn, where I heard that Privy Councillor Schulze was lodging (— I naturally took rooms at the Blue Star) — I luckily met him and, after he had already arranged everything for his departure today, persuaded him to stay with me until this evening; we were both greatly pleased to meet.... This morning I went with Schulze first to Böttiger, then to the picture gallery, then to Böttiger’s lecture, where we went through the antiquities again."}}],"created":1795220786,"model":"qwen","system_fingerprint":"b11429-d81235049","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_tokens":297,"prompt_tokens":402,"total_tokens":699,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0}},"id":"chatcmpl-pbYIqPxh5HWmASLPVUkk179LGfCSzmx2","timings":{"cache_n":0,"prompt_n":402,"prompt_ms":529.196,"prompt_per_token_ms":1.316407960199005,"prompt_per_second":759.6429300297054,"predicted_n":297,"predicted_ms":6874.132,"predicted_per_token_ms":23.223418918918917,"predicted_per_second":43.05998197299674}}